{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3004","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3004","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3004\",\"parent_revision\":\"afd11f249f102ae8ca9acf048b1db2c2885f909be1bd7f70642031e5b9c91a53\",\"root_revision\":\"afd11f249f102ae8ca9acf048b1db2c2885f909be1bd7f70642031e5b9c91a53\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_core/gh_client.py` defines `DH_LABELS: dict[str, str]` (around line 88) as a registry of status labels, but it is under-used \u2014 roughly 19 raw `\\\"status:X\\\"` string literals exist elsewhere in the same file instead of referencing `DH_LABELS`. Worse, the registry does not span languages: `.github/workflows/quality-gate-audit.yml` line 23 hardcodes a second, independent copy \u2014 `const VERIFIED_LABEL = 'status:verified'` \u2014 in JavaScript. Nothing keeps these three sources (the enum-shaped intent of `DH_LABELS`, the raw literals in `gh_client.py`, and the JS constant in the workflow) in sync; a renamed or added status label can drift undetected across any of them.\\n\\nThis repo already solved an analogous problem for section names: PR #2987 introduced `backlog_core/section_registry.py` with `SectionKey`/`SubsectionKey` `StrEnum`s plus `SECTION_NAME_ALIASES`/`SUBSECTION_NAME_ALIASES` alias maps and `resolve_section_name`/`resolve_subsection_name` functions, then `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_section_roundtrip_integrity.py` added a grep-based round-trip/membership test extending that pattern to catch drift.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A `StatusLabel` `StrEnum` (or equivalent canonical registry) is added to `backlog_core`, replacing `gh_client.py`'s under-used `DH_LABELS` dict and its ~19 raw `\\\"status:X\\\"` literal duplicates with references to the enum.\\n- [ ] A test (grep-based, extending the pattern already established in `test_section_roundtrip_integrity.py` \u2014 not a general duplicate-literal linter, which was considered and rejected as too noisy for legitimately-repeated literals like test fixtures and docstrings) verifies that every status label referenced anywhere in the repo (Python, YAML, JS) is a member of the canonical `StatusLabel` set, so a renamed/added label that isn't propagated everywhere fails CI instead of drifting silently.\\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/quality-gate-audit.yml`'s hardcoded `VERIFIED_LABEL = 'status:verified'` JS constant is replaced or validated against the same canonical source (e.g. generated from the Python enum, or covered by the new round-trip test so a mismatch is caught).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer maintaining backlog_core**, I want to **replace raw `\\\"status:X\\\"` string literals with a canonical `StatusLabel` registry (StrEnum + alias map), mirroring the `SectionKey`/`SubsectionKey` pattern already established in `backlog_core/section_registry.py`**, so that **status labels have one source of truth instead of drifting silently across Python and workflow-YAML/JS copies**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Identified during a self-directed workflow-quality review of the `development-harness` plugin (2026-08-18), adversarially reviewed by a second agent before filing. User-provided context (candidate directions surfaced during investigation, not a required approach) \u2014 the enum + grep-based round-trip test approach is the recommended direction; a general-purpose duplicate-literal linter was explicitly considered and rejected (too much noise on legitimate repeats, and structurally blind to cross-language copies like the JS constant).\\n- **Related**: #2911 addresses duplicated *function logic*, not this raw string-literal/no-registry problem \u2014 confirmed via full-body read to not overlap.\\n- **Precedent**: `backlog_core/section_registry.py` (PR #2987) and `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_section_roundtrip_integrity.py` (PR #2986) are the direct templates for both the registry shape and the test pattern.\\n- **Process note**: Filed via `gh issue create` rather than the `/dh:work-backlog-item create` skill \u2014 that skill's gate-token bang-exec line fails deterministically in this session's worktree (tracked separately as #2992).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f6027cb1acbd6381f48b53c2539fb118cb4efceb235b68d51070a247d3935f7f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiITAQ\"}"}